elad-spectrum (1.0.0-2) bookworm; urgency=medium

  [ Spectrum Display ]
  * Red tuned frequency marker line with off-screen arrow indicator
  * Frequency, mode and filter bandwidth overlay (cyan, centered)
  * Band overlay on frequency axis (green=ham, orange=broadcast, gray=other)
  * ITU Region 1, 2 and 3 band plan files (JSON)
  * Adjustable reference level and dynamic range
  * VFO A/B indicator in spectrum frame label

  [ Waterfall Display ]
  * Local and UTC time display overlay (top-left and top-right)
  * Filter bandwidth indicator lines (dashed, red/orange by mode)
  * Mode-aware bandwidth positioning (USB/LSB/CW/AM/FM/Data)
  * Orange bandwidth lines for CW resonator modes

  [ CAT Control ]
  * Filter bandwidth display via RF CAT command
  * Immediate frequency query on connect
  * Serial port auto-reconnection on device power cycle

  [ USB Reconnection ]
  * Automatic detection of USB disconnection
  * Auto-reconnection with FPGA FIFO re-initialization
  * libusb context reinitialization for clean state recovery
  * Stabilization delay for FPGA initialization after power-on

  [ Zoom and Pan ]
  * Horizontal zoom (1x, 2x, 4x, 8x, 16x) with pan support
  * Pan step scales with zoom level (one grid line per detent)
  * SPAN and OFS display in kHz

  [ Raspberry Pi Mode ]
  * Dual rotary encoder support via libgpiod
  * Encoder 1: cycle and adjust spectrum/waterfall ref/range
  * Encoder 2: toggle between zoom and pan modes
  * Compact parameter display with active parameter highlighting
  * Dark theme forced in Pi mode, system theme otherwise

  [ Settings ]
  * Persistent settings saved to ~/.config/elad-spectrum/settings.conf
  * Debounced auto-save (3 seconds after last change)
  * Save on exit

  [ UI Polish ]
  * Colored status indicator (green=connected, gray=disconnected, red=error)
  * Removed frame borders for cleaner appearance
  * Right-justified axis labels
  * Increased font sizes for spectrum and waterfall axes

  [ Packaging ]
  * Debian package includes band plan files for all three ITU regions
  * Developer and user documentation

 -- Michel, VE2EXB <ve2exb@mikelachaine.ca>  Sun, 08 Feb 2026 12:36:00 -0500

